        <briefdescription>
<para>Normalize the distribution. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Combines multiple edges to the same <emphasis><ref refid="structllvm_1_1_block_frequency_info_impl_base_1_1_weight_1a7d49b2704586051c51172cc77d4104b3" kindref="member">Weight::TargetNode</ref></emphasis> and scales down so that <emphasis>Total</emphasis> fits into 32-bits.</para>
<para>This is linear in the size of <emphasis>Weights</emphasis>. For the vast majority of cases, adjacent edge weights are combined by sorting <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_block_frequency_info_impl_base_1_1_distribution_1a3009a397a01cea6f6903433da6683224" kindref="member">WeightList</ref> and combining adjacent weights. However, for very large edge lists an auxiliary hash table is used. </para>
